1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:02,964
What if every farmer in India
stopped working for a week?

2
00:00:03,034 --> 00:00:05,444
Nearly half of India's
workforce is in farming.

3
00:00:05,565 --> 00:00:08,035
They grow the food for one
point four billion people.

4
00:00:08,065 --> 00:00:10,355
The first thing to vanish
wouldn't be rice or wheat.

5
00:00:10,451 --> 00:00:14,101
Government godowns hold grain stocks,
and those would last a while.

6
00:00:14,121 --> 00:00:15,311
It would be the fresh things.

7
00:00:15,412 --> 00:00:17,452
Milk, vegetables and fruit don't wait.

8
00:00:17,452 --> 00:00:20,982
By day two, mandis would be
empty and city prices would jump.

9
00:00:21,057 --> 00:00:24,847
In twenty eighteen, farmers in
several states held a ten day protest,

10
00:00:25,217 --> 00:00:28,007
and some cities felt the
shortage of vegetables and milk.

11
00:00:28,078 --> 00:00:30,128
A nationwide strike would be far bigger.

12
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:31,398
Then the fields themselves.

13
00:00:31,629 --> 00:00:34,799
Crops left unwatered or
unharvested would start to spoil.

14
00:00:34,884 --> 00:00:37,954
Everything we eat comes from
someone who woke up before sunrise.

15
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:40,889
So what if every farmer in
India stopped for a week?

